Open Vanilla 0029: action-bar range colour only for spells that can take the selected unit (client).
IsActionInRange answered "out of range" (0, a red icon) for a buff such as Arcane Intellect while a far
enemy was selected, although pressing it casts the buff on yourself. The reference's IsActionInRange
(0x4e56f0) runs CanTargetUnit (0x6e4440) first, which binds the selection: a spell that cannot take the
selected unit (a buff with an enemy selected, a bolt with a friend) answers nil, like having no target.
feed_action_state now runs the same bind test (cast_target::unit_binds) before the range test; without
the faction table it falls back to the distance alone. Test: a_spell_that_cannot_take_the_selected_unit_has_no_range_answer.

